      "title": "Junior Manager Talent & Careers (Temporary)",
      "description": "Junior Manager Talent & Careers (Temporary) in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Junior Manager Talent & Careers (Temporary) Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 11 hours ago (03/09/2026 12:52) Job ID 2026-3174 # of Openings 1 Category Talent & Careers Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Talent & Careers is looking for an Junior Manager (Temporary) to join its team! IE University is seeking a highly motivated and organized Junior Manager of IMBA Talent & Careers to provide temporary support to the International MBA (IMBA) Talent & Careers team during a period of sick leave. The successful candidate will contribute to the team’s day-to-day operations by developing presentations, preparing employability reports, and assisting students with their queries. This role requires strong communication, analytical, and organizational skills, as well as the ability to collaborate effectively with internal stakeholders and work in an international environment. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in María de Molina 11 Responsibilities Your role as a Junior Manager will involve: Create and update high-quality presentations and supporting materials for the IMBA Talent & Careers team. Adapt content for different audiences, ensuring that all materials are accurate, clear, engaging, and aligned with IE University standards. Collaborate with team members to gather, organize, and present relevant career-related information. Update and maintain IMBA-related information, resources, and content on the Career Portal. Coordinate with relevant stakeholders to identify and implement necessary content updates. Collect, organize, review, and consolidate employability information from different sources. Help ensure the accuracy and consistency of the data used for internal and external reporting. Support the preparation of employability reports, presentations, and other data-driven materials. Assist in responding to students’ questions regarding Talent & Careers services, resources, and processes. Provide clear, timely, and student-focused guidance, escalating more complexmatters to the appropriate team member when necessary. Contribute to delivering a positive and consistent student experience throughout the IMBA program. Provide ongoing operational and administrative support to the IMBA Talent & Careers team. Coordinate with colleagues and other internal departments to support the effective delivery of career-related initiatives. Manage multiple priorities and contribute flexibly to emerging team needs. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Education, Communication, Human Resources, or a related field; a Master’s degree is preferred. 0-2 years of relevant professional experience in higher education, career services, project coordination, human resources, or a related area. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Full professional proficiency in English is essential; Spanish proficiency is a strong advantage. Strong organizational skills and proven ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities in a dynamic environment. Strong attention to detail and good analytical skills and experience preparing reports and working with data. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft PowerPoint and Excel. Familiarity with digital platforms, content management systems, or career management platforms is an advantage. Strong interpersonal skills and a collaborative, proactive, and service-oriented approach. Valie EU work permit. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3174/junior-manager-talent-%26-careers-%28temporary%29/job?in_iframe=1 6"
