    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3172/program-assistant%2c-school-of-science-%26-technology/job": {
      "title": "Program Assistant, School of Science & Technology",
      "description": "Program Assistant, School of Science & Technology in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Program Assistant, School of Science & Technology Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 12 hours ago (03/09/2026 10:54) Job ID 2026-3172 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's School of Science and Technology is looking for an Program Assistant to join its team! The Program Assistant is responsible for the delivery and day-to-day management of the program. This includes acting as the primary point of contact between students, professors and various IE internal stakeholders and departments, as well as all related communications with them; implementing guidelines and policies; supporting program logistics and operations; supporting faculty members; and helping in all student-related services. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Program Assistant will involve: Interaction with Students: Meet with students to solve issues, offer advice, and/or give support on a daily and regular basis. Collaborate with class representatives in coordination with, and under the supervision of, Directors and Managers. Support students in solving simple technical issues. Manage (written and oral) communication to students, including all written regular communications and information points; presentations and information sessions; etc. and communication of IE regulations (exemptions, attendance, exam dates). Management of extracurricular and curricular internships. Attend class representative meetings and help preparing the corresponding reports. Interaction with Professors and other departments: Liaise with professors to communicate specific student or group situations, request feedback, ensure timely submission of grades, syllabi, etc. Remind professors of key deadlines and follow up on pending items such as syllabi, grades, and meeting minutes. Ensure excellent student experience throughout the program by supporting professors in the delivery of sessions/exams (e.g., external proctoring service coordination, assisting with virtual classes, etc.). Collaborate with other IE Departments – such as the Administration Department, Admissions Department, Marketing Department, Planning, Documentation, Student Services, Student Life, Registrar’s Office, Maintenance Dept., etc. – to ensure a successful student experience. Manage the logistics of the program deliveries: caterings, organisation of extracurricular events (dinners, visits, etc.) and travel arrangements Contribute to the preparation and edition of internal and expenses reports. Internal Development: Assist the Directors in the implementation of new curricular and extracurricular innovations. Collaborate in the organization and management of events and initiatives within the school, ensuring smooth logistics and effective communication. Take ownership of special program components, areas, initiatives, and projects. Maintain and enhance academic guides and all other materials for students and faculty. Manage all non-academic aspects of the program on a day-to-day basis. Generate, update and make program calendars available to Faculty and Advisors through the online Campus. Foster a learning community around course topics by maintaining regular communication with alumni, experts, and faculty. Administrative support for the development of innovative learning methodologies and tools. In collaboration with Academic Directors and internal Faculty, helping to organize, and schedule panels for final project presentations, and ensure that students, faculty, and advisors are informed of the dates. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelors degree preferred. Strong proficiency in English, native preferred; Spanish proficiency helpful but not required. Excellent organization skills, detail-oriented and multi-tasking. Strong desire to work in a multicultural environment, enjoy interacting with students, and provide outstanding customer service. Basic knowledge of audiovisual equipment is an asset. Valid EU work permit. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3172/program-assistant%2c-school-of-science-%26-technology/job?in_iframe=1 9"
