    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3166/technology-junior-manager%2c-operations-%28temporary%29/job": {
      "title": "Technology Junior Manager, Operations (Temporary)",
      "description": "Technology Junior Manager, Operations (Temporary) in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Technology Junior Manager, Operations (Temporary) Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 4 days ago (31/08/2026 09:30) Job ID 2026-3166 # of Openings 1 Category Talent & Careers Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Operations Technology Team is looking for an Technology to join its team! Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a proactive and detail-oriented professional to join the Talent & Careers team on a temporary basis, covering a maternity leave. This role will support the Operations and Technology function, ensuring the smooth execution of key processes related to career services platforms, data management, and user support. This is a highly data-driven role. The candidate will work extensively with Excel on a daily basis, managing and transforming data across systems. The ideal profile is comfortable handling large datasets, working with digital tools, and collaborating with multiple stakeholders in a fast-paced environment. Responsibilities Your role as a Technology Junior Manager will involve: Platform Support & User Assistance Provide day-to-day support to students, alumni, and internal teams using the Career Portal (12Twenty) and related tools Troubleshoot technical issues and escalate when needed Assist in maintaining platform content and ensuring data accuracy Data Management & Quality ControlPerform data cleaning, validation, and consistency checks across systems Manage data uploads, imports, and exports (primarily using Excel) Ensure alignment and synchronization between platforms (e.g., Career Portal, CRM, reporting tools) Reporting & Analytics Support Assist in generating reports and dashboards (e.g., Power BI) Support data extraction, transformation, and preparation for analysis Help monitor key KPIs and performance indicators Project & Process Support Support ongoing projects such as platform migrations, integrations, or feature rollouts Document processes and contribute to improving operational workflows Collaborate with different teams (Employer Relations, Advising, Operations) Testing & Continuous Improvement Participate in testing new features or system updates Identify opportunities to improve processes and user experience Provide feedback on system performance and usability Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree Previous experience in operations, data management, or technology-related roles Skills Advanced Excel skills (mandatory): strong proficiency working with large datasets, formulas (e.g., VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, pivot tables), and data cleaning/structuring. This is a core requirement for the role Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Ability to learn new systems quickly Problem-solving mindset and proactive attitude Strong communication skills in English (C1 or above) Tools (nice to have): Power BI or similar reporting tools SQL or basic database knowledge Azure or cloud-based environments CRM systems (e.g., Microsoft Dynamics) Career platforms (e.g., 12Twenty, Symplicity) Microsoft Office Suite (advanced Excel expected) Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3166/technology-junior-manager%2c-operations-%28temporary%29/job?in_iframe=1 11"
