    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3165/associate-director-%26-talent-partner/job": {
      "title": "Associate Director & Talent Partner",
      "description": "Associate Director & Talent Partner in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Associate Director & Talent Partner Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 4 days ago (31/08/2026 09:15) Job ID 2026-3165 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Talent Management team is looking for an Associate Director & Talent Partner to join its team! The Associate Director of Talent Management will contribute to the design and implementation of the talent management programs aimed at developing and engaging high performing staff according to IE´s mission and values. They will also carry out a function as Talent Partner, being the direct point of contact for the international teams and the commercial areas of the business for the recruiting, learning & development and performance management processes. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as an Associate Director and Talent Partner will involve: Support the annual strategic planning process for the Talent Management function. Review and analyze business requests to identify trends and recommend solutions to improve employee development and value proposition. Coordinate and follow-up on the training & recruitment needs of the different business areas. Liaise with the recruitment team and business areas to ensure optimal progress of the recruitment processes according to the objectives and standards defined for the different teams. Develop and consolidate yearly analyses of key people metrics. Collaborate in the implementation and continuous development of all stages of the performance management cycle. Identify and implement technological improvements for the Talent Management function. Ensures compliance and alignment with IE´s Talent Management policies within the different departments. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Master´s degree, preferably within the field of Human Resources or similar. Bilingual in Spanish and English. 2+ years HR related experience ideally in the education sector. Stakeholder management experience within an international environment. Great communication and presentation skills. Team player with a “can do” attitude. Excellent customer orientation and organization skills. Experience with Talent software Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3165/associate-director-%26-talent-partner/job?in_iframe=1 0"
