ce Review, or Journal of Politics. The postdoctoral position is 100% focused on research. It offers a competitive remuneration package, resources for conference travel, and an enriching and cosmopolitan work environment in the heart of Madrid. Successful candidates will mainly collaborate on and contribute to articles related to the project, with a focus on the empirical work packages. The project provides the opportunity to design research and collect original data, through surveys, field work, or elite interviews. Postdocs are encouraged to also pursue their own lines of research. Successful candidates will become members of the (DIS)EMPOWER project team and join the Political Science and International Relations group within IE SPEGA, which consists of 18 tenured and tenure-track scholars studying comparative politics, international relations, political economy, and political behavior. The IE SPEGA is part of IE University, located in Madrid and Segovia, Spain. We are a fast-growing department committed to world-class academic research and teaching in the social sciences, public policy, and international affairs. Our working language is English, and both our faculty and student body are highly diverse and international. IE University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and strongly encourages applications from individuals who will expand the diversity of our faculty. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as Postdoctoral Researcher (Mixed Methods) will involve: Collaborate on the implementation of the ERC Consolidator Project (DIS)EMPOWER and contribute to the preparation and publication of scientific articles. Conduct empirical research activities, with a primary focus on the project's empirical work packages. Design and conduct original data collection through surveys, fieldwork, and elite interviews. Analyze quantitative and qualitative data using appropriate empirical methods. Present research findings at academic conferences and contribute to the dissemination of project results. Develop independent research projects aligned with the candidate's own research agenda. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Candidates should have a PhD in political science , political economy, industrial relations or related field, or demonstrate clear evidence that PhD will be completed by the start of the position (no later than September 2027). Candidates should seek to develop their academic career, be autonomous and productive team workers. Essential skills include strong methodological skills, such as the demonstrated ability to analyze observational data to address social science questions. The position specifically requires experience doing mixed method and qualitative research, such as interviews, as well as excellent analytical and communicating skills. Our working language is English. Fluency in another language relevant for the project (French, German, Japanese, Korean, Spanish, Swedish) is an asset. Application Instructions: Applications should include a cover letter and CV, a job market paper, and three confidential letters of recommendation. The cover letter should briefly describe your research interests, relevant experience, and how you would contribute to the (DIS)EMPOWER project (max. 2 pages). Interested candidates must apply by October 30, 2026. Contact Michael Becher (michael.becher@ie.edu) if you have questions regarding the position or application process. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3160/postdoc-in-political-economy-%28mixed-methods%29/job?in_iframe=1 9"
