    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3159/cybersecurity-tech-%28colombia%29/job": {
      "title": "Cybersecurity Tech (Colombia) in Bogotá",
      "description": "Cybersecurity Tech (Colombia) in Bogotá | Careers at Bogotá, Colombia Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Cybersecurity Tech (Colombia) Job Locations CO-Bogotá Posted Date 1 month ago (04/08/2026 10:20) Job ID 2026-3159 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE's IT Department is looking for a Cybersecurity Tech to join its team! We are seeking a Cybersecurity Tech with a technical and operational background to provide cybersecurity coverage outside European business hours. The ideal candidate will be act as the main cybersecurity technical reference during non-EU hours, working closely with the European team, internal IT teams, and an external SOC provider. This is not a SOC analyst or monitoring role . It is a hands-on security engineering position , focused on incident ownership, operational decision-making, vulnerability management, and internal security testing. Why IE University? With 50 years of experience and founded by and for entrepreneurs, IE University has turned business education on its head through disruptive teaching. We count on high-level faculty who bring real-world experience into the classroom and foster a hands-on approach to learning. Our Purpose At IE University, we foster positive change through education, research, and innovation. As a transformative educational institution, we empower students to make their mark on the world. We provide them with the skills, knowledge, and environment needed to make a difference, and they join a supportive and international community that lasts a lifetime. Our spirit of innovation and entrepreneurship has allowed us to drive change and constantly stay at the cutting edge of higher education. And through diversity, we have harnessed the power of people while also understanding and embracing the importance of humanities. Our People At IE we are People-driven Change Builders Autonomy Enthusiasts Communication Enthusiasts Knowledge Champions We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Bogotá (Colombia). Responsibilities Your role as Cybersecurity Tech will involve: Act as the cybersecurity point of contact outside European business hours. Coordinate with the external SOC provider: validate alerts, make decisions, and close incidents Perform urgent security changes when required (firewalls, EDR/XDR, cloud security). Manage the vulnerability management lifecycle: scanning, validation, prioritization, and remediation follow-up. Execute security hardening actions and technical improvements outside EU business hours. Collaborate with IT, Cloud, and Infrastructure teams across LATAM and the US. Provide clear asynchronous reporting and handover to the European cybersecurity team. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should have: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Telecommunications, or a related technical field. At least 3 years of hands-on experience in managing or supporting cybersecurity platforms (SIEM, SOAR, EDR, IDS/IPS, firewalls, etc.). Solid understanding of networking, operating systems (Windows/Linux) Hands-on experience with Nessus or similar tools. Demonstrated experience in incident handling and technical documentation . Analytical mindset, attention to detail, and a “hands-on” approach. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with tools such as XDR , FW. Experience working with external SOC providers. Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment and manage multiple projects simultaneously. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3159/cybersecurity-tech-%28colombia%29/job?in_iframe=1 10"
    },
    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3158/academic-planning-%26-faculty-experience-support-officer/job": {
      "title": "Academic Planning & Faculty Experience Support Officer",
      "description": "Academic Planning & Faculty Experience Support Officer in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Academic Planning & Faculty Experience Support Officer Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (31/07/2026 11:43) Job ID 2026-3158 # of Openings 1 Category Operations Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Asset Management and Planning is looking for an Assistant, Academic Planning & Faculty Experience Support to join its team! Provide operational and administrative support to the Academic Planning & Faculty Experience function, supporting the Associate Directors in the delivery of academic planning processes, faculty coordination and academic administration. The role contributes to the efficient execution of academic operations through accurate administration, timely coordination and high-quality service. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Associate Director will involve: 1. Operational Support Provide day-to-day administrative and operational support to the Associate Directors. Assist in coordinating academic planning activities and monitoring operational tasks. Prepare and maintain documentation required to support academic operations. 2. Faculty Requests and Communications Manage the faculty mailbox, ensuring requests are accurately categorised , assigned and followed through to completion. Coordinate responses with the relevant teams and monitor resolution times. Support faculty with routine operational enquiries. 3. Academic Documentation Coordinate the collection, review and tracking of syllabi and other academic documentation. Monitor submission deadlines and follow up on outstanding items. Ensure documentation is complete and correctly recorded in institutional systems. 4. Administrative Process Management Process faculty requests and operational incidents in accordance with established procedures. Maintain accurate records and monitor ongoing cases. Escalate issues where appropriate to ensure timely resolution. 5. Academic Data Maintenance Update academic structures and planning information in institutional systems. Verify the accuracy and consistency of operational data. Support the preparation of reports and planning information. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor's degree desirable. Fluent in English and Spanish. Experience in administrative or operational support roles. Strong organisational skills and attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and institutional information systems. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3158/academic-planning-%26-faculty-experience-support-officer/job?in_iframe=1 0"
    },
    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3157/associate-director-of-academic-planning-%26-faculty-experience/job": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Academic Planning & Faculty Experience",
      "description": "Associate Director of Academic Planning & Faculty Experience in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Associate Director of Academic Planning & Faculty Experience Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (31/07/2026 11:31) Job ID 2026-3157 # of Openings 1 Category Operations Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Asset Management and Planning is looking for an Associate Director to join its team! Manage the end-to-end academic planning and faculty coordination processes for an assigned portfolio of programmes, ensuring the delivery of high-quality academic schedules, efficient resource planning and an outstanding faculty experience. The role acts as the key operational liaison between faculty, academic leadership and operational teams, ensuring academic requirements are translated into effective and sustainable planning solutions. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Associate Director will involve: 1. Academic Planning Manage the academic planning process for an assigned portfolio of programmes . Develop and maintain teaching schedules that meet academic, operational and institutional requirements. Ensure academic planning milestones and deadlines are achieved. 2. Timetable Planning and Resource Optimisation Configure and optimise academic timetables to maximise the efficient use of faculty and institutional resources. Balance faculty availability, programme requirements, classroom capacity and operational constraints. Identify scheduling conflicts and implement appropriate solutions in collaboration with key stakeholders. 3. Faculty Coordination and Experience Act as the main operational point of contact for faculty throughout the academic planning cycle. Coordinate the collection of faculty availability, teaching preferences and academic documentation. Provide guidance on planning processes, institutional procedures and digital tools. 4. Academic Information Management Ensure the accuracy, consistency and completeness of academic planning information across institutional systems. Monitor teaching allocations, planning data and documentation. Maintain high standards of data quality. 5. Cross-functional Collaboration Work closely with Programme Directors, Academic Area Directors and Operational teams. Coordinate planning changes and communicate impacts. Support institutional planning standards and best practices. 6. Continuous Improvement Identify opportunities to improve planning processes. Contribute to new tools, workflows and process improvements. Promote standardisation across academic planning. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Experience in academic operations, planning or complex operational environments. Strong organisational and analytical skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and stakeholders. Excellent communication and relationship management skills. Customer-focused mindset. Fluent in English and Spanish. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3157/associate-director-of-academic-planning-%26-faculty-experience/job?in_iframe=1 1"
