e transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Lima, Peru. Responsibilities Your role as Associate Director will involve: Increase overall awareness of IE Undergraduate programs in the Peru , Bolivia & Paraguay. Plan, manage & implement business development and commercial activities for the region to promote IE’s Undergraduate programs. Participate in appropriate recruitment and enrollment activities, including Fairs, school visits, presentations, information sessions, etc Increase the number of interested candidates in IE, thereby developing a healthy and steady pipeline of candidates. Benchmark competitors focusing mainly on their commercial activities and programs Build and nurture long-term relationships with key stakeholders in the education ecosystem, including school counselors, principals, and academic coordinators, to position IE as a preferred higher education partner. Design and implement engagement strategies (e.g., exclusive sessions, workshops, school partnerships, counselor briefings) to strengthen advocacy and referral pipelines from schools across Peru, Bolivia & Paraguay. Reports to the Office D irector, Channel Director and Regional D irector Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Our ideal candidate must have great commercial skills as well as be an advocate of technology usage to manage the candidate experience. We require : Bachelors and Master´s degree from IE University or another leading school desirable Proficiency in English is fundamental Legal authorization to work in the Peru is required Experience in an international environment Intellectual curiosity, open minded and creative Great communication skills, entrepreneurial spirit, and commercial drive Strong teamwork capability and a positive customer-oriented style Analytical and numerical skills Solution-oriented and a positive/can-do attitude Availability to travel across the prioritized markets. Experience in the education sector is not required but preferable.  Knowledge of the entrepreneurial and education sector is a plus. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3156/associate-director%2c-undergraduate-programs---global-markets/job?in_iframe=1 3"
