    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3155/marketing-specialist%2c-programs-marketing-team/job": {
      "title": "Marketing Specialist, Programs Marketing Team",
      "description": "Marketing Specialist, Programs Marketing Team in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Marketing Specialist, Programs Marketing Team Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (30/07/2026 09:57) Job ID 2026-3155 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's School of Science & Technology is looking for a Marketing Specialist to join its team! IE University is seeking a Marketing Specialist to join the Global Brand & Marketing Department. The primary responsibility of this position is to execute integrated marketing activations that support the positioning, visibility, and growth of IE School of Science & Technology's academic portfolio. The Marketing Specialist will report directly to the Senior Marketing Manager and will play a key role in bringing marketing plans to life through the execution of multi-channel campaigns, go-to-market activations, content initiatives, and customer journey optimization. Working closely with Product Marketing, Digital, Brand, Admissions, Academic and Regional teams, this role ensures consistent execution across all marketing touchpoints while continuously monitoring performance and identifying opportunities for optimization. This position requires excellent organizational skills, strong project management capabilities, attention to detail, and the ability to coordinate multiple initiatives simultaneously in a dynamic international environment. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Marketing Specialist will involve: Product Marketing & Content Develop and execute marketing strategies for the School's portfolio of science and technology programs. Create compelling marketing content across multiple channels, including web, email, presentations, brochures, landing pages, video briefs, and social media. Define clear program messaging and value propositions while ensuring consistency across all marketing touchpoints. Coordinate the development of commercial materials to support global recruitment efforts. Performance Analytics & Strategic Planning In collaboration with the School Marketing Manager, support the monitoring of program performance across the full recruitment funnel (Lead Generation, Applications, Admissions, and Enrollments), reviewing dashboards and KPIs to identify trends, conversion gaps, and potential risks. Translate marketing and recruitment data into actionable insights, proactively identifying bottlenecks and recommending optimization initiatives together with Digital Marketing, Admissions, and Recruitment teams. Support annual marketing planning by defining recruitment milestones, communication priorities, and campaign roadmaps for each program. Contribute to forecasting discussions and regular performance reviews, helping identify opportunities to maximize recruitment results throughout the year. Collaboration & Project Management: Manage multiple marketing projects, ensuring timely delivery and high-quality execution. Collaborate with Academic, Admissions, Digital Marketing, Brand, Design, Recruitment teams, and external agencies to deliver integrated marketing initiatives aligned with business objectives. Support the planning and execution of recruitment campaigns, events, webinars, and product launches. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business, Communications, Science, Engineering, Technology or related fields. 2-4 years of experience in marketing, communications, consulting, advertising or digital marketing, preferably within an international organization. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple stakeholders and several projects simultaneously in a fast-paced environment. Proactive and solution-oriented mindset, capable of anticipating challenges, identifying opportunities, and driving continuous improvement. Exceptional attention to detail. Analytical mindset with experience interpreting campaign performance and marketing metrics. Genuine interest in science, technology, engineering, mathematics or emerging innovations. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Fluent in English and Spanish. Must be eligible to work in Spain. STEM academic background (Science, Technology, Engineering or Mathematics) or demonstrated experience working with STEM-related products, services or organizations. Experience in higher education, academic marketing, or consulting environments. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3155/marketing-specialist%2c-programs-marketing-team/job?in_iframe=1 5"
