    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3153/coordinator%2c-cross-program-experience---business-school/job": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Cross-Program Experience - Business School",
      "description": "Coordinator, Cross-Program Experience - Business School in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Coordinator, Cross-Program Experience - Business School Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (04/08/2026 10:50) Job ID 2026-3153 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Business School is looking for an Coordinator, Cross-Program Experience (CPX) to join its team! SUMMARY: This role is transversal across the CPX projects in participating programs in IE Business School. KEY AUDIENCES: IE Business School master students (occasional support for specific undergraduate events) RESPONSIBILITIES: The Program Coordinator is responsible for the end-to-end delivery of selected CPX events and initiatives to multiple student audiences, translating the vision set by the team into structured, high-quality execution, all with the goal of elevating the student experience. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - María de Molina, 31. Responsibilities Your role as Program Coordinator will involve: The Program Coordinator is responsible for the end-to-end delivery of selected CPX events and initiatives to multiple student audiences, translating the vision set by the team into structured, high-quality execution, all with the goal of elevating the student experience. This role acts as the primary owner of event and selected short exchange program delivery, attending to student needs, coordinating stakeholders, managing timelines, and ensuring all components are aligned for successful implementation. The Coordinator works most closely with the following teammates to align vision and objectives for each project: Associate Director: key Dual Degree student events (typically 6 per academic year (AY), for 50-70 students per event) and incoming short exchanges (4 per AY, 30-50 students per exchange week) Junior Manager: incoming exchange student Welcome Days (2 per AY, for 20-80 students per event) Executive Director: student honors ceremonies (3 per AY for 100-200 students each) and community-building social events (4 per AY with capacities ranging from 50 students to 650 students) The activities and projects on which the CPX Coordinator will work are as follows: 1. Event Delivery to Different Groups of Students (Front Office) Deliver to different student audiences key CPX events/initiatives that form part of the student journey Conduct post-event feedback and follow-up with students and propose improvements and innovation 2. Short Exchange Programs (Front Office) Coordinate and deliver 4 incoming academic short exchange (week-long) programs to a total of approximately 120-200 students Serve as coordination point with partner schools, faculty, and student participants Lead delivery and post-program evaluation 3. Additional Responsibilities (Front Office) First line of response to general student queries about Dual Degrees, international exchanges, and other CPX initiatives Guide students in specific Dual Degree processes, in conjunction with the Associate Director Maintain and update student guides and documentation 4. AI-First Process Innovation (Back Office benefitting Front Office) Propose practical, efficiency-driven improvements that will ultimately benefit the student experience Identify opportunities to streamline workflows using AI tools Use AI to support communications, documentation, and feedback analysis Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) Event Delivery: On-time delivery (at least 95%), minimum student satisfaction score of 4,0/5,0 Short Exchange Programs: 100% delivery success, minimum student satisfaction score of 4,0/5,0 Coordination: Stakeholder alignment, low escalation rate, resulting positive qualitative student feedback AI Innovation: Measurable automation, time saved that can be dedicated to students, and adoption of innovation (estimated reallocation of time as a result of AI innovations: 10%+) Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor's Degree, Master's degree from a top university preferred. Fluency in English and Spanish required (frequent interactions with students, external providers, partner schools, and occasional presentations are required). High level of Office (especially Excel) proficiency required. Familiarity with different AI tools, including Copilot. Proficiency in project management. Minimum 3-5 years of work experience preferred, involving project coordination and client-/student-facing tasks; project management qualifications and experience are a plus. Candidates must possess a valid EU work permit. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3153/coordinator%2c-cross-program-experience---business-school/job?in_iframe=1 8"
