    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3147/associate-financial-planning-%26-analysis-manager/job": {
      "title": "Associate Financial Planning & Analysis Manager",
      "description": "Associate Financial Planning & Analysis Manager in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Associate Financial Planning & Analysis Manager Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (28/07/2026 09:53) Job ID 2026-3147 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Financial Planning & Analysis Department is looking for an Financial Planning & Analysis Manager to join its team! Under the direction of a Senior Manager, the Financial Planning & Analysis Manager contributes to the analysis, projection, and reporting of financial and operational performance across the institution. He/she will play a key role in the production of insights and control reports to support data-driven decision-making within the FP&A department . Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Financial Planning & Analysis Manager will involve: Supports in data analysis, forecasting, and performance reporting. Prepares detailed profitability and KPI analyses for management review. Ensures that financial and control data is accurately recorded and structured for internal reporting and decision support. Maintains reliable financial and performance records. Prepares and reviews a variety of reports and dashboards requiring interpretation of complex data. Contributes to the continuous improvement of control, budgeting, and forecasting processes. Collaborates with other departments to ensure the consistency and quality of financial data used in projections and strategic planning. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Finance, Economics, or related field. Master’s degree in Management, Accounting or related field should be valued. Fluency and proficiency in English and Spanish. 1–3 years of experience in Audit, Finance, Controlling, or similar analytical roles. Big4 experience is valued. Advanced Microsoft Excel skills (pivot tables, financial models, macros). Experience with Microsoft Dynamics or other ERPs / financial reporting tools. Strong analytical mindset and ability to interpret large datasets. Strong knowledge of financial and accounting principles. Solid communication skills and ability to present complex data in a clear and concise way. Capacity to work with confidential financial and personnel information. Eagerness to learn and take advantage of internal training and development programs. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! 