g impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - María de Molina 31. Responsibilities Your role as Associate Director will involve: Responsible for the daily management as well as the student information and experience throughout the progr am R esponsible for a number of transversal projects ( e.g. International e xchanges , internships, c apstone p roject , d ual d egrees…) Interaction with students and faculty either in personal face-to - face meetings, via email or oth e r platforms as well as presentations and info sessions to sections or the entire cohort. Maintain a professional and friendly, customeroriented approach in this interaction. Implement and maintain program best practices and policies. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: • Master’s degree desirable. • Good organizational skills. Attention to detail. • Fluency (written & oral) in English and Spanish is a must. • Minimum of 3-5 years of operations and/or project management experience. Good knowledge of the Higher Education industry is a plus. • Occasional international travel (1 per year) Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options