    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3132/junior-data-translator%2c-it/job": {
      "title": "Junior Data Translator, IT",
      "description": "Junior Data Translator, IT in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Junior Data Translator, IT Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (22/07/2026 14:26) Job ID 2026-3132 # of Openings 1 Category IT Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's IT DEPARTMENT is looking for a JUNIOR DATA TRANSLATOR to join its team! Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. As a Junior Data Translator, you will play a pivotal role in managing the demand for data and AI projects within one of our teams. You will act as the key liaison between technical experts and educational stakeholders, ensuring that initiatives are aligned with institutional goals, deliver measurable impact, and drive data-informed decision-making. This role requires a strong combination of business understanding, analytical thinking, stakeholder management, and hands-on technical knowledge. The ideal candidate should be able not only to translate business needs into data and AI initiatives, but also to lead or directly execute more technical projects when needed, including data analysis, ETL processes, and the preparation of datasets for insight generation. A key aspect of the role is the ability to work with a high level of autonomy, helping the team move faster, respond more effectively to business needs, and enable better activation of data across the organization. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower Responsibilities Your role as a Junior Data Translator will involve: Collaborate with business, academic, and operational teams to understand their needs and identify opportunities for data and AI applications. Translate business requirements into clear, actionable project briefs for data scientists, data engineers, AI specialists, and other technical teams. Prioritize and manage the pipeline of data and AI projects, balancing strategic goals, operational demands, and available technical capacity. Ensure effective communication between technical and non-technical stakeholders, fostering mutual understanding and alignment throughout the project lifecycle. Monitor project progress, manage timelines, coordinate stakeholders, and assess the impact of implemented solutions. Conduct statistical and analytical assessments of information to generate actionable insights that help business teams better understand, activate, and leverage data in their decision-making processes. Work with data platforms such as Microsoft Fabric to manage, transform, and prepare information for analysis, reporting, and project execution. Perform ETL processes when needed, enabling greater autonomy in technical projects and reducing dependency on other teams for certain data preparation tasks. Lead or contribute to end-to-end data projects, from understanding the business problem and transforming the required data, to performing the analysis, generating insights, and supporting implementation. Facilitate training and workshops to enhance data literacy and promote AI and data adoption among academic and business teams. Identify opportunities to improve data processes, analytical capabilities, and the overall use of data across the organization. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Degree in Data Science, Business Analytics, Engineering, Education, Economics, Statistics, or a related field. Master’s degree preferred. Experience managing data, analytics, or AI-related projects is a plus. Strong analytical and statistical skills, with the ability to interpret complex information and transform it into clear, actionable insights. Ability to connect business needs with technical solutions, translating complex data concepts into user-friendly language for non-technical stakeholders. Hands-on knowledge of ETL processes, data preparation, and data transformation. Familiarity with data platforms such as Microsoft Fabric, or similar cloud-based data and analytics environments. Familiarity with data visualization tools such as Power BI. Understanding of AI applications and their potential use in educational, academic, or business contexts. Strong communication, stakeholder management, and project coordination skills. Ability to work independently, take ownership of projects, and move initiatives forward with agility. A passion for education, innovation, and making a meaningful impact through data and AI. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3132/junior-data-translator%2c-it/job?in_iframe=1 11"
