    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3131/regional-director-latam/job": {
      "title": "Regional Director LATAM",
      "description": "Regional Director LATAM in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Regional Director LATAM Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (22/07/2026 12:41) Job ID 2026-3131 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Global Markets Department is looking for a Regional Director (LATAM) to join its team! IE University is seeking an experienced and visionary leader to join the Global Markets team in Madrid (other locations would be evaluated case by case). The Regional Director for Latin America (LATAM) will oversee the region’s offices and teams, driving market development, stakeholder engagement, and the achievement of strategic goals across Latin America. This position requires a proven leader with strong commercial acumen, cultural intelligence, and the ability to align regional execution with the institution’s global strategy. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as Regional Director (LATAM) will involve: Strategic Leadership & Regional Oversight Lead, develop, and inspire a multicultural team of Managers and local Office Directors across LATAM, fostering a high-performance, collaborative, and accountable culture. Define and execute the regional strategy to strengthen institutional visibility, brand positioning, and student recruitment across diverse Latin American markets. Oversee the operations of multiple regional offices, ensuring operational excellence, consistency, and alignment with institutional priorities. Drive organizational alignment by promoting best practices, knowledge sharing, and cross-country collaboration. Business Development & Market Growth Lead student recruitment and business development initiatives to expand the institution’s presence and impact across Latin America. Identify and prioritize growth opportunities across established and emerging markets, adapting strategies to local market dynamics and competitive environments. Leverage market intelligence, data analytics, and performance indicators to support strategic decision-making, pipeline management, and market expansion. Explore new partnerships and initiatives to strengthen long-term regional growth. Stakeholder Engagement & Internal Collaboration Act as the primary liaison between the LATAM region and headquarters, ensuring strong communication and strategic alignment. Build and maintain relationships with high schools, universities, government institutions, corporate partners, educational organizations, and alumni networks to strengthen the institution’s presence in the region. Collaborate closely with academic, admissions, marketing, alumni, careers, and corporate relations teams to deliver integrated regional initiatives. Operational & Financial Accountability Define and manage regional budgets, revenue targets, and performance indicators, ensuring sustainable and profitable growth. Monitor regional performance and implement action plans to achieve enrollment, financial, and operational objectives. Champion the effective use of institutional systems, CRM tools, and technology to improve forecasting, candidate engagement, and reporting. External Representation Represent the institution as the senior regional ambassador across Latin America at conferences, industry events, government meetings, and educational forums. Strengthen the institution’s reputation and visibility by promoting its mission, values, and academic excellence throughout the region. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Master's degree or MBA from a leading institution. 10+ years of progressive leadership experience in international business development, higher education, marketing, or commercial management, including responsibility for multi-country or regional teams. Demonstrated success leading operations across Latin America, with a strong understanding of the region's educational landscape and market dynamics. Proven ability to build strategic relationships with governments, educational institutions, corporate partners, and other key stakeholders. Strong commercial mindset with experience managing budgets, revenue targets, and business performance. Excellent leadership, communication, negotiation, and influencing skills. Full professional proficiency in English and Spanish; Portuguese would be a plus. Strategic thinker with strong analytical capabilities, resilience, adaptability, and an entrepreneurial mindset. Willingness to travel extensively throughout Latin America. Legal authorization to work in Spain Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3131/regional-director-latam/job?in_iframe=1 1"
    },
    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3129/program-coordinator-%e2%80%93-online-programs/job": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator – Online Programs",
      "description": "Program Coordinator – Online Programs in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Program Coordinator – Online Programs Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (21/07/2026 17:37) Job ID 2026-3129 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Digital Learning is looking for a Program Coordinator – Online Programs to join its team! We are seeking a highly skilled and motivated Program Coordinator to join our Operations and Course Management team, supporting a portfolio of online programs. The Program Coordinator will be responsible for carrying out academic, operational, and enrollment-related duties for online programs delivered to both B2B and B2C clients. This full-time position requires an individual who is detail-oriented, comfortable working with learning management systems, and has a natural gift for customer service. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Program Coordinator – Online Programs will involve: Support the enrollment process for online programs, coordinating with both internal and external stakeholders. Attend to administrative duties to ensure a smooth enrollment process. Provide first-level technical support to participants when needed. Execute the delivery of online programs as part of the Program Management team. Manage end-to-end delivery of synchronous and asynchronous online programs. Support participants and faculty before, during, and after the program. Execute satisfaction surveys and analyze participant feedback. Leverage learning analytics to enhance the learner experience. Build and maintain strong relationships with participants, faculty, corporate clients, and internal stakeholders. Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including Academic, Admissions, Marketing, Sales, Technology, and Finance, to ensure successful program delivery. Prepare presentations, reports, and client communications. Investigate and test innovative educational technologies, artificial intelligence, and learning analytics solutions to improve program delivery and learner satisfaction. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: 0-2 years of experience in similar roles desirable. Customer-oriented with a commitment to service excellence. Strong stakeholder management and collaboration skills. High attention to detail and an organised, methodical working style. Fluency in English (native or near-native level). High level of Spanish is desirable. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and teamwork skills. Ability to work effectively with B2B and B2C clients from diverse industries, cultures, and nationalities. Ability to work in a fast-paced, international environment and adapt to changing business needs. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to make data-driven decisions. Experience working with learning management systems or online program delivery is a plus. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3129/program-coordinator-%e2%80%93-online-programs/job?in_iframe=1 2"
