    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3127/junior-manager---strategic-employer-initiatives/job": {
      "title": "Junior Manager - Strategic Employer initiatives",
      "description": "Junior Manager - Strategic Employer initiatives in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Junior Manager - Strategic Employer initiatives Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 4 weeks ago (07/08/2026 11:56) Job ID 2026-3127 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Talent & Careers is looking for an Junior Manager — Strategic Employer Initiatives to join its team! IE University's Talent & Careers Department is seeking an Junior Manager to join the Strategic Initiatives team within the Employer Partnerships division. This cross-functional team designs, launches, and scales strategic initiatives that create meaningful professional opportunities for IE students across academic programs, including employer challenges, company engagement projects, micro-internships, experiential learning initiatives, and other innovative career development experiences. This role requires someone who is highly resourceful, agile, and execution-oriented, capable of bringing together multiple internal and external stakeholders to transform ideas into impactful initiatives. The successful candidate will help strengthen students' employability by creating innovative ways to connect them with employers and real-world professional experiences. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Junior Manager will involve: Employer Partnerships Support the employer engagement strategy for cross-sector, multi-company, and strategic single-company initiatives that enhance students' professional profiles. Design and implement scalable processes that transform ideas into institutional programs, collaborating with multiple teams across and beyond Employer Partnerships. Act as the main liaison between Strategic Initiatives and IE's schools, academic units, and corporate departments in and outside Spain. Support Talent & Careers international representatives by adapting and exporting successful initiatives, processes, and best practices that strengthen employer engagement and student employability. Coordinate meetings, projects, and events involving internal stakeholders, corporate partners, and senior executives to strengthen strategic relationships. Strategy & Operations Collect, analyze, and monitor data on employer participation, student engagement, and program outcomes to measure impact and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Prepare presentations, reports, dashboards, and communication materials for internal leadership and external partners. Act as an ambassador for headquarters-led initiatives, ensuring successful implementation across IE's international offices. Provide operational, analytical, and administrative support to the Strategic Initiatives team. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Human Resources, Education, Communications, or a related field is highly recommended. Master's degree should be valuable. 1-3 years of experience in a fast-paced, project-based environment. Full professional proficiency in English and Spanish (mandatory). Strong analytical skills with exceptional attention to detail. Experience using Canva, Figma, Adobe Illustrator, or similar design tools. Outstanding communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage confidently with students, corporate partners, faculty, and senior executives. Strong organizational and project management skills, capable of managing multiple initiatives simultaneously under tight deadlines. Proactive, service-oriented, adaptable, and committed to continuous improvement. Highly motivated, results-oriented, and comfortable working both independently and collaboratively. International mindset with the ability to work effectively in multicultural environments. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in Employer Relations, Campus Recruitment, Talent Acquisition, Career Services, Higher Education, or Human Resources. Experience coordinating multi-stakeholder projects. Familiarity with CRM systems and data reporting tools. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3127/junior-manager---strategic-employer-initiatives/job?in_iframe=1 6"
