    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3126/product-marketing-specialist/job": {
      "title": "Product Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "Product Marketing Specialist in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Product Marketing Specialist Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (21/07/2026 08:47) Job ID 2026-3126 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's School of Architecture and Design is looking for an Product Marketing Specialist to join its team! Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Product Marketing Specialist will involve: Product Marketing & Content Develop and execute marketing strategies for the School's portfolio of architecture and design programs. Create compelling marketing content across multiple channels, including web, email, presentations, brochures, landing pages, video briefs, and social media. Define clear program messaging and value propositions while ensuring consistency across all marketing touchpoints. Coordinate the development of commercial materials to support global recruitment efforts. Performance Analytics & Strategic Planning In collaboration with the School Marketing Manager, support the monitoring of program performance across the full recruitment funnel (Lead Generation, Applications, Admissions, and Enrollments), reviewing dashboards and KPIs to identify trends, conversion gaps, and potential risks. Translate marketing and recruitment data into actionable insights, proactively identifying bottlenecks and recommending optimization initiatives together with Digital Marketing, Admissions, and Recruitment teams. Support annual marketing planning by defining recruitment milestones, communication priorities, and campaign roadmaps for each program. Contribute to forecasting discussions and regular performance reviews, helping identify opportunities to maximize recruitment results throughout the year. Collaboration & Project Management Manage multiple marketing projects, ensuring timely delivery and high-quality execution. Collaborate with Academic, Admissions, Digital Marketing, Brand, Design, Recruitment teams, and external agencies to deliver integrated marketing initiatives aligned with business objectives. Support the planning and execution of recruitment campaigns, events, webinars, and product launches. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Master's degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, Design, Architecture, or a related field. 2-4 years of experience in product marketing, brand marketing, or a similar role. Excellent communication, writing, and storytelling skills. Strong project management, organizational, and analytical skills. Proactive and solution-oriented mindset, with the ability to anticipate challenges, identify opportunities, and drive continuous improvement. Strong sense of ownership and accountability, with the ability to independently move projects forward while collaborating effectively with cross-functional teams. Genuine interest in architecture, design, creativity, and higher education. Fluent in English and Spanish. Preferred Skills A keen eye for design, visual communication, and brand consistency, with an understanding of design systems. Curious, commercially minded, and proactive, always looking for opportunities to improve marketing performance. Ability to challenge the status quo, think strategically, and confidently present recommendations supported by data and market insights. Familiarity with digital marketing, CRM platforms, marketing analytics, and social media best practices. Comfortable working in a fast-paced, international environment and adapting to changing priorities. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3126/product-marketing-specialist/job?in_iframe=1 7"
    },
    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3125/advisor%2c-campus-life---student-experience/job": {
      "title": "Advisor, Campus Life - Student Experience",
      "description": "Advisor, Campus Life - Student Experience in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Advisor, Campus Life - Student Experience Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (21/07/2026 08:42) Job ID 2026-3125 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Student Experience, Campus Life is looking for an Advisor to join its team! Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid Responsibilities Your role as an Advisor will involve: Reporting to the Executive Director of Campus Life (and thereby the Vice Rector for Education & Student Experience) Maintain a welcoming atmosphere and environment, adding value to the overall Student Experience. Provide outstanding customer service to students and internal institutional teams. Provide outstanding customer service to contractors and external stakeholders. Processing expenses and invoices with the providers and the accounting department. Support with logistics for activities/events, in the IE Tower in particular, and coordinating with the IE Maintenance team accordingly. Determine and/or analyze problems that may arise, offering solutions when necessary. Maintain unparalleled working knowledge of the Student Experience network, policies & procedures, as well as offerings. Oversee planning of Campus Life meetings and team building activities. Availability on weekends to help with occasional community events that take place on campus. Handle IE Connects reimbursements & budget requests through internal platforms. Leading the database transformation project by compiling and updating databases. Contribute to the preparation and editing of internal reports by spearheading data analytics & metrics for Campus Life team. Prepare courier packages and their collection. Booking and expense management for all events/activities that require travel outside of Madrid. Support with the fluid transformation and improvement of the IE Connects Platform, specifically the “Student Community” space. Support with hospitality initiatives for new students (information sessions, focus groups, volunteer groups, surveys, as well as welcome kits when applicable). When necessary, checking and approving events created by Student Clubs in the IE Connects system. Confer with Management about any concerns/issues that arise regarding all aspects of the use IE Student Experience services/assets, especially concerning coherent messaging and communication. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Either English or Spanish as native tongue, Proficient use of the other language necessary. Excellent customer service skills with proven ability to develop and maintain strong working relationships. Extremely organized and very detail oriented. Team player, who enjoys working in a collaborative environment. Experienced in working with other cultures. Ability to work on and/or support on multiple projects within the same timeframe and under tight deadlines. Motivation to engage with University staff and students on a regular basis. Ability to work occasional weekends when needed. Flexibility in schedule. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3125/advisor%2c-campus-life---student-experience/job?in_iframe=1 9"
    },
    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3124/operational-assistant%2c-center-for-families-in-business/job": {
      "title": "Operational Assistant, Center for Families in Business",
      "description": "Operational Assistant, Center for Families in Business in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Operational Assistant, Center for Families in Business Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 2 months ago (17/07/2026 16:53) Job ID 2026-3124 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's IE Center for Families in Business is looking for an Operational Assistant to join its team! We are looking for a highly organized, proactive, and detail-oriented professional who will play a central role in the daily operations of the Center for Families in Business. This person will be the operational backbone of the Center, ensuring that activities run smoothly, deadlines are met, and stakeholders receive an outstanding experience. The ideal candidate enjoys coordinating multiple projects simultaneously, anticipates needs before they arise, and thrives in a dynamic environment that combines education, research, events, and engagement with entrepreneurial families. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as an Operational Assistant will involve: Executive & Administrative Support Manage the Director's calendar, scheduling meetings & classes , coordinating priorities, and anticipating scheduling conflicts. Prepare agendas, meeting materials, reminders, and follow-up actions to ensure effective execution. Monitor key deadlines, deliverables, and commitments Serve as a trusted operational partner by proactively identifying needs and proposing solutions. Program & Operations Management Coordinate the end-to-end execution of educational programs, ensuring a high-quality participant experience. Manage communications and logistics with faculty, participants, mentors, and external partners. Help in c oordinat ion of workshops, conferences, mentoring sessions, and high-level meetings. Support the implementation and continuous improvement of operational processes across the Center. Project & Initiative Coordination Track mentoring programs, ensuring milestones and meetings Maintain project timelines and monitor progress across the Center's strategic initiatives. Prepare and update dashboards and reports to monitor key performance indicators. Support research and educational initiatives through administrative coordination and project tracking. Communications & Materials Prepare, edit, and format presentations, reports, and documents using the Center's visual identity and templates. Ensure consistency and quality across all communication materials. Support the preparation of meeting briefs, participant materials, and internal documentation. Financial & Administrative Tracking Track budgets, invoices, reimbursements, and payments, ensuring timely processing and accurate records. Maintain organized documentation for contracts, expenses, and financial reporting. Relationship Management Act as a primary point of contact for participants, faculty, partners, mentors, and entrepreneurial families. Ensure prompt, professional, and personalized communication with all stakeholders. Foster a welcoming and high-quality experience that reflects the standards of the Center. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Fluency in English and Spanish (written and spoken). Exceptional organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritize multiple competing tasks. Strong interpersonal and communication skills . High level of autonomy, reliability, and a proactive problem-solving mindset. Ability to work across educational programs, research initiatives, events, and administrative processes. Comfortable interacting with senior stakeholders, including faculty, business leaders, partners, and entrepreneurial families. . Experience using CRM systems, project management platforms, Microsoft Office, and collaborative digital tools. Strong analytical skills and comfort working with data tracking, dashboards, and reporting. Excellent attention to detail and commitment to quality and continuous improvement. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online A