    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3114/analyst%2c-corporate-relations/job": {
      "title": "Analyst, Corporate Relations",
      "description": "Analyst, Corporate Relations in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Analyst, Corporate Relations Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (30/07/2026 10:23) Job ID 2026-3114 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Corporate Relations is looking for an Analyst to join its team! The Corporate Relations Analyst will join IE University's Corporate Relations team, supporting the development of learning partnerships with corporations, public institutions, family businesses, and international organizations across multiple industries and regions. This role offers a unique opportunity to contribute to the design of corporate education solutions that help organizations build the capabilities needed to drive transformation, innovation, leadership, and sustainable growth. Working closely with Business Developers, Key Account Managers, Academic Directors, Marketing, and Operations teams, you will contribute to the design of client solutions, market research, proposal development, and strategic initiatives while gaining exposure to the full lifecycle of corporate partnerships in an international environment. This role is designed for early-career professionals who aspire to develop into trusted advisors, supporting organizations in identifying capability needs and co-creating learning solutions that generate measurable business impact. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Corporate Relations Analyst will involve: Support the development of proposals, presentations, and client-facing materials for corporate partners. Conduct research on industries, organizations, market trends, and capability development priorities. Analyze client needs and contribute to the design of customized corporate education solutions aligned with business objectives . Collaborate with Business Developers, Key Account Managers, Academic Directors, Marketing, and Operations teams throughout the client engagement lifecycle. Prepare benchmarking studies, reports, presentations, and internal documentation that support business development activities. Leverage AI and digital tools to accelerate research, strengthen business analysis, develop high-quality proposals, presentations, and client deliverables, and improve productivity while exercising critical judgment and ensuring the accuracy, relevance, and integrity of outputs. Contribute to knowledge sharing, continuous improvement initiatives, and the development of best practices across the Corporate Relations team. Support strategic projects that contribute to client success and business growth. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration , Economics, International Relations, Engineering, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English (mandatory). Spanish is preferred. Knowledge of Arabic or additional languages such as French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Japanese, Chinese, or other European or Asian languages will be considered a strong asset. Strong analytical thinking and structured problem-solving skills. Excellent written communication and presentation skills. Ability to synthesize complex information into clear and actionable recommendations. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail. Collaborative mindset and ability to work effectively in multidisciplinary and multicultural teams. Interest in corporate education, organizational development, leadership, innovation, digital transformation, and lifelong learning. Confidence using AI and digital tools to enhance the quality and efficiency of work while exercising sound judgment and maintaining high standards of quality. International academic, professional, or extracurricular experience will be highly valued. What we're looking for We are looking for individuals who demonstrate : Intellectual curiosity and a passion for continuous learning. Strong communication and interpersonal skills . Client-oriented thinking and business acumen. Initiative, ownership, and a proactive attitude. Adaptability in fast-paced and multicultural environments. Critical thinking and sound judgment when evaluating information and AI-generated outputs. A collaborative mindset and the ability to build effective working relationships. Motivation to help organizations solve business challenges through learning and capability development. What success looks like Successful Corporate Relations Analysts combine business curiosity with structured thinking, strong communication skills, and a client-oriented mindset. They ask thoughtful questions, collaborate effectively across teams, and leverage AI responsibly to improve the quality, efficiency, and impact of their work. They demonstrate sound judgment, embrace continuous learning, and have the potential to become trusted advisors supporting organizations in developing the capabilities required to succeed in an increasingly dynamic business environment. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3114/analyst%2c-corporate-relations/job?in_iframe=1 2"
