    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3113/junior-associate-faculty-payments/job": {
      "title": "Junior Associate Faculty Payments",
      "description": "Junior Associate Faculty Payments in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Junior Associate Faculty Payments Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 1 month ago (21/07/2026 09:44) Job ID 2026-3113 # of Openings 1 Category Accounting/Finance Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Faculty Payments, Administration & Accounting is looking for a Junior Associate to join its team! The Junior Associate will ensure the efficient, accurate, and timely processing of faculty payments, delivering high-quality service and ensuring proper accounting and tax compliance across all academic payment operations. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a Junior Associate will involve: • Manage the daily faculty payment process. • Record accounting transactions (invoices, payments, transfers, etc.). • Handle tax-related procedures: tax residency, withholdings, compliance. • Verify documentation required for payment processing. • Register and update professor personal and banking data. • Reconcile academic planning and teaching schedules. • Provide support to professors via email, phone, and in person. • Coordinate with Academic Planning, IT and Vice Dean of Faculty. • Process national and international remittances and wire transfers. • Identify and resolve discrepancies in billing and payments. • Ensure all processes comply with legal and internal regulations. • Support budget planning and reconciliation. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Degree in Business Administration, Economics or Accounting. At least 1 year of experience in similar roles, ideally in academic or international environments. Knowledge of accounting and taxation applicable to professional services. Fluent in Spanish and English (spoken and written). (C1 level valued). Proficient in Microsoft Office. Experience with ERP systems (Dynamics 365 valued). Experience and willingness to learn and apply AI-driven tools (ChatGPT, Copilot, Claude, etc) in administrative and accounting processes. Strong multitasking and organizational skills; ability to perform under pressure. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. International mindset and experience in multicultural environments. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3113/junior-associate-faculty-payments/job?in_iframe=1 4"
