    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3088/associate-director%2c-marketing-%26-communications---centre-for-health-%26-well-being/job": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Marketing & Communications - Centre for Health & Well-being",
      "description": "Associate Director, Marketing & Communications - Centre for Health & Well-being in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Associate Director, Marketing & Communications - Centre for Health & Well-being Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 3 months ago (19/06/2026 11:00) Job ID 2026-3088 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Center for Health & Well- being is looking for an Associate Director, Marketing & Communications to join its team! The Center for Health & Well- being advances a holistic , evidence-based approach to helping individuals and communities thrive . Through academic programs , partnerships , research , and community engagement , the Center promotes well-being , resilience , purpose , and sustainable performance across the IE ecosystem and beyond . The Center plays an important role in supporting student development , fostering a culture of well-being , and contributing to IE University's broader mission of developing responsible , human- centered leaders capable of creating positive impact . Position Overview Reporting to the Academic Director , the Associate Director of Marketing & Communications will lead the Center's marketing, communications , and positioning strategy to strengthen visibility , engagement , and impact . This role combines strategic marketing, brand development , stakeholder engagement , communications , people leadership , and performance measurement to support the Center's growth and influence within IE and globally . The Associate Director will work closely with the Student Education & Experience vertical, IE Marketing and Communications , as well as other key stakeholders across the university to ensure alignment of messaging , campaigns , engagement strategies , and institutional priorities . The role requires a holistic perspective on the student and community experience , positioning the Center's initiatives within the broader IE ecosystem to maximize impact , strengthen collaboration , and create a cohesive experience across students , faculty, staff, alumni, and partners . While supported by interns and other resources , this position is expected to focus primarily on strategic planning , ecosystem engagement , alignment with institutional strategy , stakeholder management , and impact generation . Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as Associate Director will involve: Strategic Marketing & Positioning Develop and execute an integrated marketing and communications strategy aligned with the greater institutional strategy and the Center's mission , strategic objectives , and institutional priorities . Strengthen the Center’s brand , visibility , and thought leadership across internal and external audiences , specifically elevating IE’s relevance in human capacity education and experience Ensure the Center's marketing and communications efforts support broader student engagement , community-building , and institutional objectives . Identify opportunities to expand reach , engagement , partnerships , and strategic influence . Translate academic , research , and well-being content into compelling , accessible , and impactful communications . Identify opportunities to integrate the Center's initiatives into wider institutional campaigns , experiences , and strategic initiatives . Marketing, Communications & Engagement Lead marketing campaigns and communication initiatives that increase awareness , participation , and impact . Oversee content development across websites , digital channels , newsletters , social media, reports , presentations , events , and promotional materials . Collaborate closely with IE Marketing & Communications teams to maximize visibility , consistency , and institutional alignment . Coordinate with Student Education & Experience and other key departments to ensure a coherent and integrated approach to student-facing communications and engagement . Develop communication plans that contribute to a seamless experience across the student , faculty , staff, alumni , and partner journey . Support the promotion of academic programs , events , research initiatives , partnerships , and community activities . Stakeholder & Community Development Build and maintain strong relationships across IE and with external stakeholders to strengthen collaboration , participation , and engagement . Foster greater integration of the Center across schools , departments , centers, student-facing units , alumni relations , and corporate partners . Serve as a connector across the IE ecosystem , identifying opportunities for collaboration , amplification , and shared value creation . Support cross-functional initiatives that strengthen community engagement , belonging , well-being , and student success . Represent and advocate for the Center's mission and initiatives both internally and externally . Operations & Project Management Develop systems , processes , and frameworks that improve coordination , efficiency , scalability , and execution . Manage communication calendars , campaigns , projects , vendors , agencies, and external partners . Support budget planning , monitoring , and resource management related to marketing and communications activities . Establish workflows and governance mechanisms that facilitate collaboration across stakeholders and reduce duplication of effort . People Leadership Lead, coach, and develop marketing and communications team members , interns , and contributors . Foster a high-performing , collaborative , and well-being-centered team culture. Set priorities , objectives , and performance expectations aligned with the Center's strategic goals . Support talent development , resource allocation , and effective team execution . Analytics & Impact Define and track KPIs related to visibility , engagement , participation , partnerships , and impact . Develop dashboards and reporting mechanisms to inform strategic decision-making . Measure the effectiveness of campaigns , initiatives , and stakeholder engagement efforts . Use data, insights , and stakeholder feedback to continuously improve performance and maximize impact . Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Education & Experience Master's degree in Marketing, Communications , Business, Public Relations , Strategic Communications , or a related field . 4-6 years of relevant experience in marketing, communications , brand management , stakeholder engagement , community building , or related areas . Experience developing strategic marketing and communication plans and managing complex , cross-functional projects . Experience within higher education , foundations , research institutions , social impact organizations , or purpose-driven environments is highly desirable . Skills Strategic thinking with strong execution capabilities . Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; Spanish is highly desirable . Strong stakeholder management , relationship-building , and influencing skills . Ability to navigate complex organizational environments and build alignment across diverse groups . Strong project management and organizational skills . Data- driven decision-making and analytical capabilities . Experience with digital marketing, content strategy , communication platforms , and engagement analytics . Collaborative , proactive, entrepreneurial , and solutions-oriented mindset . Passion for well-being , human development , education , and positive social impact . Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3088/associate-director%2c-marketing-%26-communications---centre-for-health-%26-well-being/job?in_iframe=1 5"
