    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3014/fpi-predoctoral-fellowship-%28project-pid2024-155187ob-i00-kan4met%29/job": {
      "title": "FPI Predoctoral Fellowship (Project PID2024-155187OB-I00-KAN4MET)",
      "description": "FPI Predoctoral Fellowship (Project PID2024-155187OB-I00-KAN4MET) in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! FPI Predoctoral Fellowship (Project PID2024-155187OB-I00-KAN4MET) Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 2 months ago (30/06/2026 15:47) Job ID 2026-3014 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's Research Office Mathematics Department is looking for an FPI Predoctoral Fellow to join its team! PhD Predoctoral Fellowship to join the KAN4Met project and develop next‑generation AI weather forecasting models based on Kolmogorov–Arnold Networks (KANs). The research will combine deep learning, atmospheric data and HPC. We offer a fully funded FPI PhD position in the project “Kolmogorov‑Arnold Networks with applications in weather forecasting (KAN4Met)”, led by Prof. David Gómez‑Ullate. https://ieresearchdatalab.github.io/KAN4Met/ The PhD candidate will join an interdisciplinary team of mathematicians, physicists, statisticians and computer scientists working at the intersection of approximation theory, AI and atmospheric science. The goal is to understand and improve KAN architecture and to develop an AI weather prediction model for the Iberian Peninsula, inspired by the latest advances in AI forecasting. The candidate will have the opportunity to complete one or more 3‑month international research stays in top research institutions, gaining exposure, collaborations and a broader scientific perspective. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - María de Molina. Responsibilities Your role as a Fellow will involve: Analyze academic literature in management, business strategy, innovation, and platform markets to identify relevant research gaps and contribution opportunities. Implement advanced research methodologies, including statistics and econometrics, as well as empirical research related to AI and digital platforms. Develop, write, and present academic research papers at international conferences, workshops, and academic seminars. Prepare high-quality academic manuscripts for submission to peer-reviewed management and strategy journals. Collaborate with faculty and research teams on ongoing research projects within the fields of corporate strategy, competition, innovation, and AI. Contribute actively to the academic research environment of IE University, including participation in seminars and research discussions. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: RESEARCHER PROFILE: Master Required Education level: MSc/MEng in Mathematics, Physics, Computer Science or Engineering Research field:Computer Science / Applied Mathematics / Data Science / Engineering Required Languages: English (B2 requiered, C1 desirable) Knowledge of deep learning frameworks, Neural ODEs, Physics‑Informed Neural Networks, and High‑Performance Computing will be valued. Academic record, research merits and motivation to pursue a PhD will be the main criteria. The process will be based on the applicant’s CV, motivation letter and an interview. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/3014/fpi-predoctoral-fellowship-%28project-pid2024-155187ob-i00-kan4met%29/job?in_iframe=1 6"
