    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/2986/it-project-manager---technical-lead---web-portals/job": {
      "title": "IT Project Manager / Technical Lead - Web Portals",
      "description": "IT Project Manager / Technical Lead - Web Portals in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! IT Project Manager / Technical Lead - Web Portals Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 2 months ago (02/07/2026 10:00) Job ID 2026-2986 # of Openings 1 Overview Are you interested in joining a dynamic and international team of professionals to transform education? IE University's IT Department is looking for a Technical Lead - Web Portals to join its team! The Information Technology department is looking for an IT Project Manager / Technical Lead - Web Portals for Application Implementation & Maintenance Projects . The successful candidate will be in charge of the projects and maintenance services within the systems of the functional area under his/her responsibility. The candidate will have g ood communication and coordination skills since he/she will be working with other IT functional responsible (Business Partners), Users Areas, vendors and outsource IT support. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid - IE Tower. Responsibilities Your role as a IT Project Manager will involve: Initially focus on CMS-based web platforms (primarily WordPress ) and progressively support the evolution towards applications embedded in Microsoft Teams using SharePoint-based CMS and integrations with modern frontend applications (Vue, React or similar) Coordinate external development teams involved in the evolution of web portals and CMS-based platforms Lead and coordinate all projects related to his/her functional Area, from both technical and functional perspectives Coordinate the Incident Resolution Team, as well as the support to all the systems under his/her responsibility Management and oversight of the portfolio of IT providers involved in the systems that support the areas under his/her responsibility Lead end-to-end implementation of new software applications, from analysis to go-live Plan and monitor project timelines, budgets, risks, and deliverables Oversee the ongoing support and maintenance of existing applications, ensuring service levels are met Manage and maintain technical and functional documentation Identify digital process improvement opportunities and recommend suitable technology solutions Ensure application security, data integrity, and system availability Participate in the definition of system architecture and selection of new tools. Apply project management methodologies (Agile, PMI, etc.) as appropriate to the project context Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in engineering, computer science or related discipline preferred +5 years of experience in technical project management related to software development in Technology or IT solutions implementation, both in consulting companies, or IT departments. Strong communication skills to engage with technical and Business Unit stakeholders Have a sound understanding of projects and IT maintenance delivery methodologies Understanding of CMS-based architectures (WordPress and SharePoint), integrations with modern frontend frameworks (Vue, React, or similar) and basic knowledge of APIs and tools such as Postman to inspect and validate API interactions Experience with agile methodologies. Certifications will be a strong plus ( PMP, Scrum master… ) Experience in ServiceNow projects will be valued Fluent English, both written and spoken Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/2986/it-project-manager---technical-lead---web-portals/job?in_iframe=1 11"
