o become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in New York City, USA. Please keep in mind that t his position is not currently open ; it is designed to identify and connect with talented individuals interested in future opportunities at IE University. By submitting your application, you will be considered for upcoming entry-level Program Assistant roles as they become available. Responsibilities Your role as an Associate Director will involve: Drive recruitment strategies and engage prospective candidates for master’s programs. Lead or support marketing and outreach campaigns to strengthen brand presence. Organize and deliver events such as info sessions, master classes, and fairs. Build and maintain relationships with companies, alumni, and strategic partners. Collaborate with internal teams to align recruitment, marketing, and admissions efforts. Conduct follow‑ups, consultations, and outreach to guide candidate pipelines. Provide data tracking and reporting to support decision-making and strategy. Support general NYC office operations as needed. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Master’s degree in business or a related field is highly preferred. 4–6 years of relevant professional experience in fields such as business development, recruitment, marketing, higher education, or client-facing roles. Exceptional communication and presentation skills, with confidence addressing diverse audiences. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within a global, multicultural environment. Capacity for strategic thinking combined with hands-on execution. Legal authorization to work and reside in the United States. Unleash your full potential and make an impact. The next move is yours! If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. If you are no longer interested in being considered for these roles, please proceed to withdraw your application. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/2864/new-york-city---talent-pipeline/job?in_iframe=1 9"
