    "https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/2853/director---talent-pipeline/job": {
      "title": "Director - Talent Pipeline",
      "description": "Director - Talent Pipeline in Madrid | Careers at Madrid Skip to Main Content Please Enable Cookies to Continue Please enable cookies in your browser to experience all the personalized features of this site, including the ability to apply for a job. Welcome page Returning Candidate? Log back in! Director - Talent Pipeline Job Locations ES-Madrid Posted Date 5 months ago (25/03/2026 12:20) Job ID 2026-2853 # of Openings 1 Overview *This is a Talent Pipeline role. Applications will be reviewed for alignment with future openings across IE University. Discover Your Future at IE University! Are you ready to take the next step in your career within a world‑class, international academic institution? At IE University, we’re always seeking visionary leaders who want to drive impact through innovation, strategy, and meaningful global engagement. This is your chance to join our Talent Pipeline for future Director‑level opportunities —submit your application now and be among the first considered when new roles open up! Position Overview: Are you looking to launch your career in a vibrant, international academic environment? As a Director at IE University, you will play a key strategic leadership role , guiding the development, execution, and continuous improvement of initiatives across our various IE Schools and central units — including the Business School, School of Politics, Economics & Global Affairs, School of Science & Technology, School of Architecture & Design, IE Law School, and other academic and institutional departments. You will collaborate closely with senior leadership, faculty, and internal stakeholders to drive innovation, strengthen strategic projects, and ensure operational and academic excellence. This pipeline is designed for experienced professionals with a strong leadership background, typically bringing 6–10+ years of relevant experience , who are ready to shape institutional strategy, manage complex initiatives, and create high‑impact outcomes within a global, multicultural environment. Why IE University? Every story begins with a purpose, and ours has always been about people. Founded in 1973, IE University has continuously raised the bar to drive positive change through education. We believe education is more than a path to professional success; it is a catalyst for personal transformation and meaningful impact. At IE University, we place people and their potential at the center of everything we do, empowering individuals to become extraordinary. We encourage bold thinking and foster a culture where innovation, curiosity, and courage lead to real-world impact. Together, we create an environment where talent thrives, and ideas shape the future. Our mission We support students in developing impact skills to live and lead with positive impact. This ignites a ripple effect: We transform people, who then transform others, systems, society, and, ultimately, our world. Our Purpose To foster positive change. Values Cultivate the humanistic approach. Empower your entrepreneurial spirit Cherish the diversity of people, mind, and experience Drive innovation with a proactive mindset We are looking for a person to join a full-time position in Madrid. Please keep in mind that t his position is not currently open ; it is designed to identify and connect with talented individuals interested in future opportunities at IE University. By submitting your application, you will be considered for upcoming entry-level Program Assistant roles as they become available. Responsibilities Your role as Director will involve: Strategic Leadership & Institutional Alignment Lead the definition, implementation, and monitoring of strategic plans within the department or center. Provide direction for long‑term development, innovation, and organizational growth. Contribute to senior management discussions, strategic decision‑making, and cross‑departmental alignment. Program, Research, or Innovation Development Design, coordinate, and enhance initiatives related to learning innovation, research programs, academic quality, or operational effectiveness. Support the development of programs, faculty experience, methodologies, and educational/operational models. Promote adoption of emerging tools, technologies, or methodologies. Operational Excellence & Problem‑Solving Oversee key processes, ensure smooth operational delivery, manage challenges, and identify improvement opportunities. Lead investigations, analyze issues, and design feasible, sustainable solutions to operational or academic problems. Coordinate resource allocation, procurement, and workflow optimization. Stakeholder, Partnership & External Engagement Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, faculty, program teams, and external partners. Represent the department in institutional meetings, academic networks, events, or external collaborations. Expand visibility and strengthen outreach, impact, or fundraising efforts when applicable. Team Leadership & Resource Management Supervise team members and lead multidisciplinary groups. Foster a collaborative environment, aligning team capabilities with institutional priorities. Ensure quality of deliverables, adherence to timelines, and consistent communication. Insight, Research & Continuous Improvement Identify trends, emerging practices, and opportunities for innovation. Promote evidence‑based decision‑making, data‑driven analysis, and high‑quality academic or operational outputs. Qualifications To thrive in this role, you should possess the following qualifications: Master’s degree from a top university required; PhD preferred, depending on area. 6–10+ years of relevant professional experience in higher education, learning innovation, public policy, academic development, operations, problem‑solving, or research environments. Proven experience managing complex projects and working with senior‑level stakeholders. Strong strategic thinking, analytical acumen, and problem‑solving abilities. Excellent organizational, leadership, and team‑management skills. High capacity for stakeholder engagement, communication, and cross-functional collaboration. Experience in innovation, research, instructional design, edtech, policy‑oriented research, or operational excellence is valued depending on the area. Fluency in English required; proficiency in Spanish highly preferred. If you want to be part of this educational revolution, we invite you to apply and be part of our dynamic team at IE University. At IE University, we actively promote equal opportunities in recruitment processes and access to employment, always ensuring the absence of gender, sexual orientation, religion, age, ethnic origin, or disability bias throughout the entire selection process. If you are no longer interested in being considered for these roles, please proceed to withdraw your application. Options Apply for this job online Apply Share Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Join Our Talent Community! Looking for an amazing career opportunity, but just not seeing exactly what you want? We are always looking for top talent and we are interested in connecting with you in the future! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com https://careers-ieedu.icims.com/jobs/2853/director---talent-pipeline/job?in_iframe=1 4"
